  "prefLabel": "Plc 902.05 Cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR)",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 902.05 “Cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR)” means a procedure involving repeated compression of a patient’s chest, performed in an attempt to restore the blood circulation and breathing of an individual who has suffered cardiac arrest.\n\nSource. #14387, eff 10-17-25, EXPIRES: 10-17-35",
